"type":"text","text":"Runs depth-first searches with a growing depth limit that keep only the current path, so states"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"need only be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and memory stays proportional to the path. A path never revisits a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state on itself. Returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when no goal is reachable and the space is finite; on an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"infinite space without a goal, it does not return."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"With no record of visited states, every path is enumerated again at each depth, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exponential in the depth on graphs with many routes between states (a grid). Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)"},{"type":"text","text":" when states are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and memory allows."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A shortest path by edge count from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"start"},{"text":" to the first state satisfying ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isGoal"},{"text":", by iterative","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deepening.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/traversal\/iterativedeepeningdepthfirstsearch(from:successors:until:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal"]]},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Traversal\/SuccessorFunctionSearch.swift#L77","fileName":"SuccessorFunctionSearch.swift"},"symbolKind":"func","roleHeading":"Function","role":"symbol","title":"iterativeDeepeningDepthFirstSearch(from:successors:until:)","modul